    <item>
  <title>FDA Launches New Program to Advance Neuroscience Medical Product Development </title>
  <link>http://www.fda.gov/news-events/press-announcements/fda-launches-new-program-advance-neuroscience-medical-product-development</link>
  <description>FDA announces the launch of the Neuroscience Advancement and Innovation Nexus (NAIN), a new agency program aligned with the Trump Administration’s efforts to accelerate medical innovation and deliver breakthrough treatments. </description>
  <pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:58:19 EDT</pubDate>
    <dc:creator>FDA</dc:creator>
    <guid isPermaLink="true">http://www.fda.gov/news-events/press-announcements/fda-launches-new-program-advance-neuroscience-medical-product-development</guid>
    </item>
<item>
  <title>FDA Approves First-of-Its-Kind Chronic Hepatitis B Treatment </title>
  <link>http://www.fda.gov/news-events/press-announcements/fda-approves-first-its-kind-chronic-hepatitis-b-treatment</link>
  <description>FDA today approved Hibsago (bepirovirsen) injection, in combination with existing antiviral therapy, to treat chronic hepatitis B virus (HBV) infection in certain adults without cirrhosis.</description>
  <pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:40:38 EDT</pubDate>
    <dc:creator>FDA</dc:creator>
    <guid isPermaLink="true">http://www.fda.gov/news-events/press-announcements/fda-approves-first-its-kind-chronic-hepatitis-b-treatment</guid>
    </item>
<item>
  <title>FDA Approves Once-Weekly Generic Hormone Therapy Patch for Women</title>
  <link>http://www.fda.gov/news-events/press-announcements/fda-approves-once-weekly-generic-hormone-therapy-patch-women</link>
  <description>Today, the U.S. Food and Drug Administration approved the first generic of Climara Pro (estradiol and levonorgestrel transdermal system, 0.045 mg per day/0.015 mg), a transdermal hormone therapy patch for women with an intact uterus applied once a week.</description>
  <pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 11:57:36 EDT</pubDate>
    <dc:creator>FDA</dc:creator>
    <guid isPermaLink="true">http://www.fda.gov/news-events/press-announcements/fda-approves-once-weekly-generic-hormone-therapy-patch-women</guid>
    </item>
<item>
  <title>FDA Issues Final Guidance on Prescription Drug Apps and Software</title>
  <link>http://www.fda.gov/news-events/press-announcements/fda-issues-final-guidance-prescription-drug-apps-and-software</link>
  <description>The U.S. Food and Drug Administration today released final guidance establishing a clear framework for how drug companies can develop, distribute, and label apps used alongside their prescription medicines.</description>
  <pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 09:03:14 EDT</pubDate>
    <dc:creator>FDA</dc:creator>
    <guid isPermaLink="true">http://www.fda.gov/news-events/press-announcements/fda-issues-final-guidance-prescription-drug-apps-and-software</guid>
    </item>
<item>
  <title>FDA Approves Immunotherapy That May Allow Certain Patients with Rectal Cancer to Avoid Chemotherapy, Radiation and Surgery</title>
  <link>http://www.fda.gov/news-events/press-announcements/fda-approves-immunotherapy-may-allow-certain-patients-rectal-cancer-avoid-chemotherapy-radiation-and</link>
  <description>The U.S. Food and Drug Administration today granted accelerated approval for a new use of the immunotherapy Jemperli (dostarlimab-gxly) that may allow some patients with locally advanced rectal cancer to avoid common treatments that can have a lasting impact on their daily life.</description>
  <pubDate>Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:19:38 EDT</pubDate>
    <dc:creator>FDA</dc:creator>
    <guid isPermaLink="true">http://www.fda.gov/news-events/press-announcements/fda-approves-immunotherapy-may-allow-certain-patients-rectal-cancer-avoid-chemotherapy-radiation-and</guid>
    </item>
<item>
  <title>FDA Launches the Rare Disease Framework Initiative to Develop a Holistic, Fit-For-Purpose Framework for Rare Disease Drug Development</title>
  <link>http://www.fda.gov/news-events/press-announcements/fda-launches-rare-disease-framework-initiative-develop-holistic-fit-purpose-framework-rare-disease</link>
  <description>The U.S. Food and Drug Administration, a division within the U.S. Department of Health and Human Services (HHS), today announced the Rare Disease Framework Initiative to reimagine the development of drugs and biologics for rare diseases. </description>
  <pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 11:50:52 EDT</pubDate>
    <dc:creator>FDA</dc:creator>
    <guid isPermaLink="true">http://www.fda.gov/news-events/press-announcements/fda-launches-rare-disease-framework-initiative-develop-holistic-fit-purpose-framework-rare-disease</guid>
    </item>
<item>
